
@attribute [Route(GlobalValues.Path_Nav_Group_Overview)]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Page_Title_Nav_Group_Overview_Test</PageTitle>

<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class @GlobalValues.Info_Box_Coloured_Modifier">
    <h1 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Nav Group Overview & Tests</h1>

    <p>
        This Nav Group component is designed to be used in a side navigation HTML <strong>nav</strong> element. It provides the ability to create 'N'-level deep navigation systems, with 
        eech section being able to contain links or other sections and so on.
    </p>
    <p>
        Each expanding section (an un-ordered list of links or other sections) is based on the disclosure pattern and as such uses a button to show or hide its content. As the content just pushes content below it out of the way
        as opposed to being a dropdown that obsures content beneath it no special keyboard support has been added.
    </p>
    <p>
        <b>Released: </b>Current version <b>v1.0.0</b> See the documentation site for more information: <a target="_blank" class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" href="@GlobalValues.Site_Link_Docs_Nav_Group">Nav Group documentation (opens in new window)</a>
    </p>
</section>
<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class">

    <h2 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Information & instructions</h2>
    <p>
        Below is a single Nav Group component which, in this instance has been configured with two nested sections, Components and Nav Group. The only content within the Components section is the 
        Nav Group section. This section only contains two links, Nav Group Overview & Tests (which has the url to this, the current page) and the Nav Group Quirks & Issues link which if activated 
        would take you to that page on this site. 
    </p>
    <p>
        Using the keys as descirbed below, navigate to each section and to the links. As not to be taken away from the page do not activate the links.
    </p>
    <h2 id="tabs-keyboard" class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Keyboard interaction</h2>
    <ul aria-labelledby="tabs-keyboard">
        <li>
            <kbd>Tab</kbd> - when focus moves into the Nav Group, places focus onto the the first focusable element which could be a link or a section (button for the disclosure).
        </li>
        <li><kbd>Shift + Tab</kbd> reverses tab direction.</li>
        <li><kbd>Up Arrow</kbd> - moves focus to the previous accordion heading. If the focus is on the first heading, moves focus to the last heading.</li>
        <li><kbd>Space or Enter</kbd> - when on a section expands or collapses that section.</li>
        <li><kbd>Enter</kbd> - when on a link activates it.</li>
    </ul>

</section>

<section class="section-box">
    <nav aria-label="navigation example">
    <NavGroup>
        <NavSection SvgIcon="--svg-component-icon" Title="Components" Expanded="false">
            <NavSection SvgIcon="--svg-open-book-icon" Title="Documentaion" Expanded="false">
                    <NavGroupLink SvgIcon="--svg-article-icon" Href="@GlobalValues.Path_Nav_Group_Overview" LinkText="Nav Group Overview & Tests" TargetType="TargetType.Self" />
                    <NavGroupLink SvgIcon="--svg-article-icon" Href="@GlobalValues.Path_Nav_Group_Quirks" LinkText="Nav Group Quirks & Issues" TargetType="TargetType.Self" />
            </NavSection>
        </NavSection>
    </NavGroup>
</nav>
</section>

<div class="flex-content justify-content-between">
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Left_Arrow_Modifier" href="@GlobalValues.Path_Modal_Dialog_Quirks">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Main_Nav_Section_Heading_Modal_Dialog - @GlobalValues.Page_Heading_Modal_Quirks</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Right_Arrow_Modifier" href="@GlobalValues.Path_Nav_Group_Quirks">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Main_Nav_Section_Heading_Nav_Group - @GlobalValues.Page_Heading_Nav_Group_Quirks</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
</div>
@code {

